] "\n\n" [:p {} "Many top players did compete, however, including " [:a {:href "/athletes/134013"} "Justin Rose"] ", " [:a {:href "/athletes/136017"} "Henrik Stenson"] ", and the American foursome of " [:a {:href "/athletes/136308"} "Rickie Fowler"] ", " [:a {:href "/athletes/136305"} "Bubba Watson"] ", " [:a {:href "/athletes/136306"} "Matt Kuchar"] ", and " [:a {:href "/athletes/136307"} "Patrick Reed"] ". After two rounds, relatively obscure Australian " [:a {:href "/athletes/132506"} "Marcus Fraser"] " led over Belgian " [:a {:href "/athletes/132675"} "Thomas Pieters"] " and the critics were up again, saying that the tournament was hurt by the absence of so many top players. However, Rose was in third and Stenson was fourth, and when Fraser and Pieters stumbled in round three, Rose took the lead with Stenson second. Stenson shot 68 in the final round, but could not catch Rose, who fired 67 to win by two shots. Kuchar was another shot back in bronze medal position. With an exciting final two rounds, enthusiastic galleries, and three medalists who were acknowledged to be among the top players in the world, many of the complaints about Olympic golf seemed ill-founded."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "Strokes"] [:th {} "To Par"] [:th {} "Round #1"] [:th {} "Round #2"] [:th {} "Round #3"] [:th {} "Round #4"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/134013"} "Justin Rose"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/GBR"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/GBR.png"}] "GBR"]] [:td {} "268"] [:td {} "-16"] [:td {} "67 (=4)"] [:td {} "69 (=12)"] [:td {} "65 (2)"] [:td {} "67 (=8)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/136017"} "Henrik Stenson"]] [